<title>GERMANY: German cocoa grind sharply lower in Q4, 1996.</title>
<headline>German cocoa grind sharply lower in Q4, 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German cocoa grind dropped by 21.2 percent to 56,254.7 tonnes in fourth quarter 1996 from 71,375.0 tonnes in the same 1995 period, the German Confectionery Industry Association BDS said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Analysts earlier this week estimated the data to be down by some two percent from comparable 1995, citing a weak economic climate but allowing for compensation from chocolate exports.</p>
<p>The German grind total for the whole year stands at 251,069.4 tonnes, three percent down from 1995's total 258,816.7 tonnes.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
